# SQL's `GROUP BY`: DS0105 explaining `summarize ... by`.
mode: syntax
---- query
'orders.csv' | GROUP BY customerId
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..35
  PIPELINE@0..34
    LITERAL@0..12
      STRING@0..12 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
    PIPE@13..14 "|"
    WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
    ERROR@15..34
      IDENT@15..20 "GROUP"
      WHITESPACE@20..21 " "
      IDENT@21..23 "BY"
      WHITESPACE@23..24 " "
      IDENT@24..34 "customerId"
  WHITESPACE@34..35 "\n"

error[DS0105]: SQL keyword `GROUP BY` is not an operator
  --> query:1:16
  |
1 | 'orders.csv' | GROUP BY customerId
  |                ^^^^^^^^ this is SQL
  |
  = help: to group rows, use `summarize ... by`: `summarize count() by customerId`
